# Mandatory-review paths. See docs/adr for the decisions behind this setup.
#
# CODEOWNERS applies to the *last* matching pattern, so more specific rules
# should stay below more general ones if that behavior is ever relied upon.
# For now these six are independent (non-overlapping) path prefixes.
#
# `crates/duels-eval/**` and `crates/duels-value/**` are here for a different
# reason from the other three. Neither is documentation or configuration: each
# is a shared asset that at least one agent's *measured strength* depends on
# directly - `duels-eval` for the rest of the ladder, `duels-value` for the
# champion (`mcts-value`) specifically - and a change to either moves that
# agent's strength at once. Everything else in this repository can be reviewed
# by reading the diff; these crates have to be reviewed by asking "was this
# measured?". The rule exists to stop their behaviour being changed in passing
# inside a PR that is nominally about something else.

docs/**                @kncesarini
.github/**             @kncesarini
data/**                @kncesarini
crates/duels-eval/**   @kncesarini
crates/duels-value/**  @kncesarini
CODEOWNERS             @kncesarini
